.TH CRS\-TUNNEL 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-tunnel \- manage ssh tunnels to the control room VNC sessions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-tunnel
.IR open | close | status | connect
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR H ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-viewer
.IR BIN ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crs\-tunnel
opens, closes, probes, or attaches to ssh tunnels carrying the control
room VNC traffic.
Each session in
.B controlroom.yaml
maps a client-side
.I local_port
to
.I 5900+display
on its DAQ host, routed through the gateway with
.B ProxyJump
and authenticated with Kerberos (GSSAPI).
One master ssh per session keeps a control socket in
.BR ~/.crs/ ,
so tunnels survive and can be probed
.RB ( "ssh \-O check" )
or closed
.RB ( "ssh \-O exit" )
without pkill.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B open
Open the tunnel(s).
Requires a valid Kerberos ticket
.RB ( "klist \-s" ).
.TP
.B close
Close the tunnel(s) via their control sockets and remove stale sockets.
.TP
.B status
Print one line per session: state, local port mapping, account.
Defaults to
.B \-\-all
when no target is given.
.TP
.B connect
Open the tunnel if needed, then launch a VNC client against the local
port. On macOS this runs
\fBopen vnc://localhost:\fIPORT\fR
(the built\-in Screen Sharing client); elsewhere it runs
.BR "vncviewer \-Shared" .
An explicit
.B \-\-viewer
overrides this on any platform.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-session " NAME"
Operate on one named session.
.TP
.BI \-\-host " H"
Operate on every session on a host (short or FQDN).
.TP
.B \-\-all
Operate on every configured session.
.TP
.BI \-\-config " FILE"
Path to controlroom.yaml (default: ./config/, or
.BR CRS_CONFIG ).
.TP
.BI \-\-ssh\-config " FILE"
Alternate ssh config passed as
.BR "ssh \-F" ;
used by the test harness to alias cluster hosts to localhost.
.TP
.BI \-\-viewer " BIN"
VNC viewer binary for
.BR connect .
Overrides the macOS
.B open vnc://
default.
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
    crs\-tunnel open \-\-all
    crs\-tunnel status
    crs\-tunnel connect \-\-session dcs\-main
    crs\-tunnel close \-\-host mu2e\-mgr\-01
.EE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.crs/ssh\-ctrl\-*
SSH control sockets, one per open tunnel.
.TP
.B config/controlroom.yaml
Central session/gateway configuration.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-remote (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR ssh (1)
.SH REPOSITORY
.UR https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-controlroom-setup
https://github.com/Mu2e/mu2edaq-controlroom-setup
.UE
